{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/206013-help-making-some-gang-related-krewes","id":206013,"title":"Help making some Gang related Krewes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-23T06:44:17-07:00","id":206013,"title":"Help making some Gang related Krewes","content":"So, I'm building a Detroit setting and I'm kind of stumped. I've created Krewes and NPCs for every aspect of the city except one very important baseline: the gangs.<br /> <br /> I want to create three distinctive gangs, and Krewes assosciated with them. The thinking being that the gangs see the Krewes as some elite wing of the gang that even the leadership is afraid of. For the most part the gangs will represent the baseline mooks of the city with even the assosciate Krewes being kind of low level and thuggish compared to the smaller, more powerful Krewes that are unaffiliated. But I'm having a bit of difficulty coming up with interesting and distinctive personas for each Krewe. I have some thoughts as to what I might do, but any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T11:29:26-07:00","id":206343,"title":"","content":"That's cool that you are doing a Detroit setting. I'm a resident of Michigan and would love to see what you have done with the D!<br /> Anyways, I would recommend looking at some of the gangs from the Saints Row series. Each of them is kind of strange...not like RL gangs (at least to my knowledge). The Sons of Samedi in particular from SR2 would be great, and I bet the Brotherhood could do the trick as well. They are all visually distinct, have some interesting personalities leading them, and I think they are ripe for the picking for the WoD.<br /> Good luck!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T17:30:10-07:00","id":209598,"title":"","content":"Remember that the Insane Clown Posse, and therefore Juggalos, originate in Detroit.<br /> Remember that the FBI classified Juggalos as a gang back in 2009.<br /> Remember that Joseph Bruce A.K.A. Violent J of ICP said that the group's mythology of a Hell-carnival and &quot;Joker Cards&quot; was inspired by a dream of &quot;spirits in a traveling carnival&quot; that he had the night after the group decided to revamp their &quot;ICP&quot; initials (from &quot;Inner City Posse&quot; to &quot;Insane Clown Posse&quot;)<br /> <br /> I <i>highly </i>recommend a Krewe of risen Juggalos, and the local Underworld taking on some of the Dark Carnival's symbolism (you don't have to listen to ICP to get this stuff, a cursory Wikipedia-ing of any of the albums in their &quot;Joker Card Saga&quot; will give you some inspiration for Kerberoi)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2709-quatrevingts","name":"QuatreVingts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2709_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T08:42:01-07:00","id":220248,"title":"","content":"The suggestions so far are great ideas. My post is more of a warning. Do yourself a favor when doing anything that<br /> may eventually make it onto the Internet involving gangs and/or the Mafia.<br /> <br /> Make. It. Up.<br /> <br /> You don't ever want information that is tied to those groups linked to you both from the standpoint of mistaken FBI<br /> searches as well as &quot;clean up crews&quot; (note the proper spelling and not game related topic). Keep this in mind for<br /> games as well as straight up fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is just my bright, shiny two cents.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing. I try not to argue in forums. It's like pouring concrete in a river. It doesn't get you anywhere in the short term and it poisons the environment long term.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2668-asmenedas","name":"Asmenedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2668_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}